<report>
<title>Fisher's exact test</title>

<p><b>Input table:</b></p>
<table>
<tr><td>@tab_a1</td><td>@tab_b1</td></tr>
<tr><td>@tab_a2</td><td>@tab_b2</td></tr>
</table>

<p><b>Arranged table and totals:</b></p>
<table>
<tr><td>@tab3_a1</td><td>@tab3_b1</td><td><subtotal>@tab3_c1</subtotal></td></tr>
<tr><td>@tab3_a2</td><td>@tab3_b2</td><td><subtotal>@tab3_c2</subtotal></td></tr>
<tr><td><subtotal>@tab3_a3</subtotal></td><td><subtotal>@tab3_b3</subtotal></td><td><grandtotal>@tab3_c3</grandtotal></td></tr>
</table>

<p>Expectation of A = @{exp_a:roundu}</p>

<p><pval>One sided @tail_1 @{p_1:pval}   (doubled one sided @{p_1d:pval})</pval><br />
<pval>Two sided @tail_2 @{p_2:pval}</pval></p>

<p><pval>One sided mid-@{mid_p:pval}</pval><br />
<pval>Two sided mid-@{mid_p_2:pval}</pval></p>
</report>